      `Old Navy's women's division has eight size charts. They are all the same chart.`,
      `The waist figures are identical, size for size, across bottoms, tops, belts, robes, underwear and swim. The chest figures are identical across tops, robes, swim and bras. The hips figures are identical across bottoms, underwear and swim. What changes between categories is which two or three rows Old Navy chooses to show you.`,
      `That matters for a practical reason. A brand that drafts swimwear, denim and bras from one body model is telling you that its published numbers describe a body, not a garment. Two Old Navy items in the same size are cut for the same measurements regardless of what they are, so the chart cannot help you judge how any particular garment will actually fit.`,
