      `Five slips across fifteen tables is what hand-copying looks like. These charts are not generated from one source of truth; they are transcribed from each other, and the transcription is imperfect. The Sleeve-versus-Arm-Length split between outerwear and shirts points the same way: a generated chart would not call one measurement two names inside a single division. That's worth knowing before you treat any single cell as authoritative.`,
