    text: [
      `Subtract waist from hip and something becomes visible.`,
      `From 000 through 14, the difference is <strong>exactly 10½ inches</strong> at every single size. Then it moves: 10¼ at size 16, 10 at size 18, and 9½ from size 20 onward, where it locks and holds at 9½ through 22, 24, 26, 28 and 30.`,
      `So Old Navy is really working from three body models under one chart. A constant-difference range through 14, a three-size transition, and a plus range built on a shape a full inch straighter through the hip than the core sizes. Nothing on the page mentions this.`,
