          ['XL', '38–41', '40–42'],
          ['XXL', '42–45', '44–46'],
        ],
      },
      `A 38-inch waist is an <strong>XL at Gap and an L at Old Navy</strong>. And Old Navy's first missing inch, 35, is the exact inch at which Gap opens its L.`,
      `The women's side has a crossover. Against <a href="/size-guides/gap-size-chart-fit-guide/" class="${linkClass}">Gap's women's bottoms chart</a>, Old Navy runs half an inch smaller at the waist from size 00 through 12, meets Gap exactly at <strong>size 14</strong> (both 33½), and runs larger above it, reaching two and a half inches apart by size 20. So "I'm a 12 at Gap" and "I'm a 12 at Old Navy" mean slightly different bodies, and which direction the difference runs depends on which side of 14 you're on.`,
      `Two smaller differences worth having: numeric size 000 is XXXS at Old Navy and XXS at Gap, and Old Navy's men's chest runs consistently larger than Gap's at the same letter, widening from one inch at M to three inches at XL.`,
    ],
  },
